  "text": "Beneath the lamps’ ethereal, pale light,\nHe walked the streets in dead of night.\nEach footfall echoed, stark and clear,\nOn pavement cold, devoid of cheer.\n\nLike ghosts, the passing figures glided,\nBy private worlds and thoughts abided.\nNo glance was cast, no word was spoken,\nIn urban sea, he stood alone.\n\nA profound solitude took hold,\nA story of the self untold.\nAmidst the crowd, he felt the chill,\nOf solitude’s enduring will.\n\n***\n\nThe animal known for its long neck is the **giraffe**."
